    skos:prefLabel 'wave overtopping events'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An amount of water flowing over the crest of a coastal structure (such as a seawall, dike, breakwater etc) due to wave action. Wave overtopping events can be assessed by measuring individual occurences or counts, measuring the volume V per overtopping wave, or by measuring the mean discharge q over a certain time interval and per meter run.'@en ;
